# Line endings are load-bearing here, not cosmetic.
#
# The brand generators pin `newline="\n"` so their SVG output is byte-identical
# on every OS, and the test suite compares generated bytes against the committed
# copies to catch stale artwork. Git for Windows ships `core.autocrlf=true` in
# its *system* config, which would rewrite those files to CRLF on checkout and
# fail the comparison on Windows while passing in CI.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the working tree to LF everywhere, so the guards mean the same
# thing on every machine.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch these — Git's binary detection is good but explicit is safer for
# the brand assets, which are compared byte-for-byte.
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
